  "cautions": [
    "The Form I resurrection sense is preserved because the lexical evidence explicitly discusses a Quranic reading for that use; the supplied canonical Form I occurrence locations themselves show spreading or opening.",
    "In the expression associated with 77:3, the spreaders are interpreted variously as angels scattering rain or winds spreading clouds or rain.",
    "نُشُور in 25:47 is lexically explained as daytime activity and going forth, even though the supplied contextual English gloss uses “a resurrection.”"
  ],
